  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 29-layer planar dielectric filter stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Materials are Ta2O5 (Gao) and SiO2 (Lemarchand) in alternating sequence with a central SiO2 (Lemarchand) defect cavity at layer 15. Layers 1-12 and 18-29 are fixed at quarter-wave optical thickness nominal values (Ta2O5 (Gao): 185 nm, SiO2 (Lemarchand): 268 nm at 1550 nm). Layers 13, 14, 15, 16, 17 are free variables with bounds ±25% around nominal quarter-wave values. Maximize mean transmittance at 1550 nm. Minimize mean transmittance in 1400-1500 nm band. Minimize mean transmittance in 1600-1700 nm band. Use coherent smatrix solver at normal incidence. Apply L2 regularization penalty on thickness deviations from nominal.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize thicknesses of five central layers (13-17) in a 29-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 Bragg mirror on fused silica to maximize transmission at 1550 nm while suppressing transmission in the 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm stopbands, using coherent scattering-matrix formalism at normal incidence.",
